nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007\ntitle: Complete QB-A editorial acceptance evidence\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nClose the one incomplete design-evidence boundary found by `GC0001`: the\nfinite QB-A catalogue has a grammar, source policy, quota tables, lifecycle,\nadjudication, and anti-repeat fixtures, but `QB-A-01` through `QB-A-48` are\nstill `draft` and have only pending reviews. Create or review durable editorial\nacceptance evidence for the existing four bounded batches only. Do not add\ncards, change quiz scope, create code/B/R runbooks, or accept the manifest.\n\n## Exact pending reasons retained from GC0001\n\n- `GPI-001`: the grammar requires a resolvable provenance record and two\n  distinct accepted current-revision reviews, but it contains no completed\n  card-level records for `QB-A-01`\u2013`QB-A-48`.\n- `GPI-002`, `GPI-003`, `GPI-004`, and `GPI-005`: each of the four named\n  12-card QB-A batches is explicitly recorded as `status: draft`,\n  `revision: 1`, with `PROV-<ID>` and two pending review records. No card may\n  become eligible from those placeholders.\n- `GAME-002`: the required original-expression, factual-source/provenance,\n  factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, and independent second\n  review decisions have not been accepted for any current card revision.\n- `GAME-004` and `GAME-006` retain their deterministic policy/fixture evidence,\n  but their use of published catalogue candidates remains conditional until the\n  preceding batch records are accepted.\n\nThere are no blocked product decisions in this wave. Implementation coverage\nremains deferred until `F012`.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/qba-editorial-acceptance-register.md`: exactly 48\n  card-level records for the existing `QB-A-01`\u2013`QB-A-48`, grouped into the\n  existing four named 12-card batches. Each record must identify the current\n  revision, original-expression/non-copying decision, durable permitted source\n  locator and checked date for every factual assertion, conflict/correction\n  state, factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, independent second\n  review, and resulting lifecycle status.\n- Update `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md` only as\n  needed to point to the register and replace the explicitly pending catalogue\n  state after all 48 records qualify. Preserve its existing quotas, IDs, and\n  source policy.\n\nThe successor must leave rejected, unresolved, withdrawn, conflicted, or\nincompletely reviewed cards ineligible and state the exact reason. It must not\nset `planning/game-design-manifest.json` to accepted. A later `GQ` audit is the\nonly task allowed to run the dedicated completion check, update canonical\nbible/inventory records, and accept that manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- All 48 existing QB-A card revisions have independently inspectable\n  original-expression, provenance, and two-distinct-review evidence, or every\n  remaining ineligible card has its exact pending or blocked reason retained.\n- The four existing batches remain finite at 12 cards each and no unreviewed\n  record can enter selection.\n---\ntask_id: GC0001\nsequence: 4\ndependencies: G0001,G0002,G0003,G0004,G0005\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.json,planning/game-production-inventory.md,planning/game-production-inventory.json,planning/game-design-manifest.json\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GAME-005,GAME-006,GAME-007,GAME-008,GAME-009,GAME-010,GAME-011,GAME-012,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007,GPI-008,GPI-009,GPI-010,GPI-011,GPI-012,GPI-013,GPI-014,GPI-015\ntitle: Check game-design coverage and dependencies\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nWrite a durable coverage-checkpoint audit for the five completed G tasks and\ntheir design evidence. Preserve the manifest as pending while its QB-A\neditorial boundary remains incomplete. The checkpoint is successful when it\nrecords that boundary accurately and `GD0002` owns the one bounded successor\nwave. Do not rewrite this GC0001 task file; write the audit to\n`design-evidence/gc0001-coverage-checkpoint.md` instead.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `design-evidence/gc0001-coverage-checkpoint.md`: the coverage, ownership,\n  dependency, pending-boundary, and successor audit for this checkpoint.\n- `GD0002.md`: the sole bounded successor for the recorded QB-A editorial\n  acceptance work. It already exists and must remain the only successor.\n\n## Existing audit findings to preserve in the output\n\n## Ownership, cap, coverage, and dependency closure\n\n| Owning batch | Declared G outputs | Cap | Canonical coverage | Closure result |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `GB0001` | `G0001`, `G0002` | 2 of 5 | `GAME-001`\u2013`004`; `GPI-001`\u2013`007` | `G0002` depends on `G0001`; closed. |\n| `GB0002` | `G0003`, `G0004` | 2 of 5 | `GAME-005`\u2013`008`; `GPI-008`\u2013`011` | `G0003` depends on `G0002`; `G0004` on `G0003`; closed. |\n| `GB0003` | `G0005` | 1 of 5 | `GAME-009`\u2013`012`; `GPI-012`\u2013`015` | `G0005` depends on `G0004`; closed. |\n\nEach G declares the same `design_authoring_batch` as its owning GB output\nlist. The selected canonical sets are covered exactly once by those batch\nallocations: all `GAME-001`\u2013`GAME-012` and `GPI-001`\u2013`GPI-015` are assigned.\nNo rejected or decision-gated module is allocated.\n\n## Detailed-evidence inspection\n\n- `G0001` supplies card grammar, original-expression policy, permitted-source\n  policy, quota tables, provenance fields, and a two-review workflow for all\n  four QB-A batches. Its 48 inventory records are nevertheless expressly\n  `draft`, with `PROV-<ID>` placeholders and pending review records.\n- `G0002` supplies deterministic select/true-false/ordered/typed adjudication,\n  20 fixtures, withdrawal/correction lifecycle states, and seeded anti-repeat\n  and shortage fixtures. Publication-dependent selection remains conditional\n  while no QB-A card is eligible.\n- `G0003` supplies `TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05` First Whistle transitions, Mixed Fixture\n  seeded selection/shortage fixtures, optional-off timer, offline and\n  interruption lifecycle, and accessibility review.\n- `G0004` supplies the capped 100-point score/streak rule, wrong/blank/timeout\n  and abandon recovery, idempotent results/milestones, edge fixtures, and text,\n  non-colour, captioned/muted audio-equivalent feedback.\n- `G0005` supplies touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad mappings; non-audio\n  and non-colour equivalents; recovery/offline/update states; and shared-rule,\n  shared-content, shared-save web/PWA/Android/iOS parity evidence.\n\n## Exact pending reasons\n\n- `GPI-001` has no completed card-level resolvable provenance plus two distinct\n  accepted current-revision reviews for `QB-A-01`\u2013`QB-A-48`.\n- `GPI-002`\u2013`GPI-005` each remain a finite 12-card `draft` batch at revision 1,\n  with placeholder provenance and two pending reviews. No placeholder can enter\n  selection.\n- `GAME-002` lacks accepted original-expression, factual-source/provenance,\n  factual/rights, accessibility/copy, and independent second-review decisions\n  for every current card revision.\n- `GAME-004` and `GAME-006` have deterministic policy and fixture evidence,\n  but use of published QB-A candidates remains conditional on the preceding\n  accepted records.\n\nThere are no blocked product decisions in this wave.\n\n## Successor decision\n\nBecause selected production entries lack accepted detailed evidence, the sole\nbounded successor is [`GD0002.md`](GD0002.md). It retains the preceding pending\nreasons and is restricted to a 48-record editorial acceptance register for the\nexisting four 12-card batches. Do not create `GQ0001.md` until that successor\ncloses e