bjective\n\nRead `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../INITIAL.md`, `../specification/00-domain-discovery.md`,\n`../specification/01-game-identity.md`, `../specification/02-game-design-bible.{md,json}`,\n`../specification/01-creative-direction.md`, and\n`../planning/game-production-inventory.{md,json}`. Maintain\n`../planning/game-design-manifest.json` as the completion gate; it starts\npending and must not be marked accepted by this dispatcher.\n\nCreate no more than three bounded GB writers, one per selected module, plus\n`GC0001.md`. Register each new file's normal Supervisor metadata and output\npaths. Each GB writer may create at most five focused `G####.md` tasks, and\nevery G task must declare its actual `design_authoring_batch: GB####`.\n\nFor this football-trivia programme, allocate design evidence for: original\nquestion-card grammar and four named QB-A editorial batches with sources and\nreviews; adjudication/fairness and anti-repeat rules; First Whistle, Mixed\nFixture, score/streak/results rules; guided accessibility, recovery/offline,\nand target parity. G tasks must create/review detailed bibles, not code and not\nimplementation B/R runbooks.\n\n`GC0001` must check G ownership, the five-G-per-GB limit, canonical GAME and\nGPI coverage, dependency closure, original-expression/provenance evidence,\nasset/audio accessibility equivalents, output quality, and manifest\nconsistency. If any selected module or production entry lacks accepted detailed\nevidence, create exactly one successor `GD####` dispatcher for the next bounded\nwave. When all required evidence is accepted, create a final `GQ####` audit.\nOnly that audit may update the canonical bible/inventory and set manifest\n`status: accepted`, accepted `final_audit`, accepted module entries with output\npaths/GAME IDs/GPI IDs, and empty pending/blocked arrays after running the\ndedicated manifest completion check. The implementation-coverage validator is\nexplicitly deferred until F012. Do not create B or R files.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `GB0001.md`: only `G0001.md` and `G0002.md` for quiz content/editorial integrity.\n- `GB0002.md`: only `G0003.md` and `G0004.md` for round/score/progress rules.\n- `GB0003.md`: only `G0005.md` for accessible recovery and target parity.\n- `GC0001.md`: validates this wave and conditionally creates exactly one next `GD` or `GQ` file.\n- `../planning/game-design-manifest.json`: remains pending; this dispatcher records planned ownership only.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The generated G collection is bounded, batch-owned, and covers every selected module and GPI entry without expanding rejected/decision-gated scope.\n- `GC0001` and later GD/GQ work provide the required validation, dispatch, and final-audit loop.\n- The manifest cannot become accepted until durable G evidence, complete module/GAME/GPI coverage, and the dedicated completion check all pass.\n---\ntask_id: GB0001\nsequence: 2\ndependencies: GD0001\nsource_specifications: specification/02-game-design-bible.md,specification/02-game-design-bible.json,specification/01-creative-direction.md\nsource_catalogue_ids: GAME-001,GAME-002,GAME-003,GAME-004,GPI-001,GPI-002,GPI-003,GPI-004,GPI-005,GPI-006,GPI-007\ntitle: Author quiz editorial design runbooks\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate only G0001 and G0002. Keep their ownership to GAME-001\u2013004 and GPI-001\u2013007; require original wording, factual source/review records, format/difficulty quotas, answer adjudication, and anti-repeat evidence.\n\n## Output list\n\n- `G0001.md` only; it must declare `design_authoring_batch: GB0001` and create/review `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md`.\n- `G0002.md` only; it must declare `design_authoring_batch: GB0001` and create/review `design-evidence/adjudication-and-freshness-bible.md`.\n\nDo not create code, B/R runbooks, copied questions/copy, or accept the manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- No more than five G tasks are 